##DESCRIPTION
##  Mental Math problems using any technique
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('mental math', 'integers')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Integers')
## DBsection('Mental Math')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('5/3/2020')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

# The following prevents answers from containing operations.
Context('LimitedNumeric');

$a1 = random(21, 49);
$b1 = 10 * random(2, 4) + non_zero_random(-1, 1);
$c1 = 100 * random(12, 20);
$d1 = 25 * random(21, 49);
$e1 = 10 * random(2,  9);
$e2 = 100 * random(3, 9);

BEGIN_PGML

Answer the following addition problems using any mental math technique:

a. [`9 \times [$a1]=\;`] [__]{Compute(9*$a1)}
b. [`[$b1] \times 99=\; `] [__]{Compute(99*$b1)}
c. [`[$c1] \div 25=\; `] [__]{Compute($c1/25)}
d. [`[$d1] \div 5=\; `] [_]{Compute($d1/5)}
e. [`[$e1] \times [$e2]=\; `] [__]{Compute($e1*$e2)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a. Use the multiply by 9 technique:
[``` 9 \times [$a1] = (10-1) \times [$a1] = [$a1*10] - [$a1] = [$a1*9] ```]
b. Since 99 is close to 100, we do something similar. 
[``` [$b1] \times 99 = [$b1] \times (100-1) = [$b1*100]-[$b1] = [$b1*99] ```]
c. Dividing by 25 can be done by multiplying by 4, then dividing by 100. 
[```[$c1]\div 25 = 4 \times [$c1] \div 100 = [$c1*4] \div 100 = [$c1/25]```]
d. Dividing by 5 can be done by mulitplying by 2, then dividing by 10.
[``` [$d1] \div 5 = 2 \times [$c1] \div 10 = [$d1*2] \div 10 = [$d1/5]```]
e. Multiples of 100 can be done by keeping track of the multiples.
[``` [$e1] \times [$e2] = [$e1/10] \times 10 \times [$e2/100] \times 100 = 
[$e1/10] \times [$e2/100] \times 10 \times 100 = [$e1*$e2/1000] \times 1000 = [$e1*$e2] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
